# Temple Digital Services Platform — Cursor Project Rule

Before performing project work, always read:

- /docs/AI_CONTEXT.md
- /docs/MODULE_STATUS.md

For module learning and implementation also follow:

- /docs/LEARNING_PROMPT.md

## Permanent Rules

- Work only on the currently approved module.
- Never automatically implement future modules.
- Follow the architecture, security, testing, reliability and cost rules in AI_CONTEXT.md.
- Use MODULE_STATUS.md as the source of truth for current project progress.
- Explain the plan before significant implementation.
- Inspect only files relevant to the current task.
- Minimize unnecessary repository scanning and token usage.
- Do not regenerate unchanged files.
- Do not perform unnecessary refactoring.
- Never hard-code or expose passwords, API keys, AWS credentials, tokens, private keys or production secrets.
- Prefer local and low-cost resources before paid cloud infrastructure.
- Never automatically run terraform apply, terraform destroy or destructive cloud commands.
- Test important changes.
- Troubleshoot failures systematically instead of applying random fixes.
- Consider security, scalability, availability, observability, reliability and cost where applicable.
- Update /docs/MODULE_STATUS.md after each module.
- Suggest a Git commit message after completing a module.
- Never automatically start the next module.
- Stop and wait for developer approval.

## Learning Workflow

LEARN
→ DESIGN
→ IMPLEMENT
→ TEST
→ BREAK SAFELY
→ TROUBLESHOOT
→ FIX
→ DOCUMENT
→ EXPLAIN
→ COMMIT